notion-recorder (1.0.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * Autostart daemon is now edge-triggered instead of level-triggered. It starts
    the bridge when external mic capture rises from zero, and after a manual Stop
    it stays stopped until the mic goes idle and re-arms. Stop is no longer
    immediately overridden while an app still holds the mic (e.g. a browser that
    keeps the mic open after a call).
  * Daemon ignores benign level monitors when deciding if you are in a meeting:
    corked source-outputs and "Peak detect" VU meters such as the GNOME Settings
    Sound panel no longer count as mic activity.

 -- samuelrawrs <54682777+samuelrawrs@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 05:00:00 +0000

notion-recorder (1.0.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Refresh routes now adapts to the live default output: when the bridge is on
    it re-points system audio at the current default sink (rebuilding only the
    output loopback) and confirms the result with a toast, instead of just
    re-reading state.
  * Hardening: UID-scoped runtime dir with 0700 perms when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is
    absent, avoiding a predictable shared /tmp path for lock and state files.
  * Release pipeline: isolate the GPG signing key from the third-party deploy
    action, pin actions to commit SHAs, drop to least-privilege token
    permissions, and publish SHA256SUMS with the release.

 -- samuelrawrs <54682777+samuelrawrs@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 26 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0000

notion-recorder (1.0.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: guided no-echo meeting mix for Notion AI Meeting Notes,
    live level meters, friendly device pickers, audio-flow diagram, an optional
    mic-activity auto-start daemon, and an optional system-tray icon to start or
    stop the mix from the top bar.

